The teacher has a total of 17 worksheets to grade, and each worksheet contains 7 problems. She has already graded 8 of these worksheets. 

To determine how many problems remain to be graded, we follow these steps:

1. **Find the number of worksheets left to grade:**
   $$
   17 \text{ total worksheets} - 8 \text{ already graded} = 9 \text{ worksheets left}
   $$

2. **Calculate the total number of problems remaining to grade:**
   Each of the 9 remaining worksheets has 7 problems, so:
   $$
   9 \text{ worksheets} \times 7 \text{ problems per worksheet} = 63 \text{ problems}
   $$

Thus, the teacher has to grade **63** more problems.

$$
\boxed{63}
