$$
9 + 27 = 36 \text{ shirts}
$$

By the time school started, he had washed 20 shirts. To find out how many shirts he did not wash, we subtract the number of shirts he washed from the total number of shirts:

$$
36 - 20 = 16
$$

Thus, the number of shirts Dave did not wash is:

$$
\boxed{16}
